  "worked_solution": "We are given the following situation for each year: \n\n- $42%$ of people who used trains swap to cars. This implies that $58%$ of them remain using trains.\n\n- $33%$ of people who used cars swap to trains. This implies that $67%$ of them remain using cars.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Trains** | **Cars** |\n| To: | **Trains** | $0.58$ | $0.33$ |\n| **Cars** | $0.42$ | $0.67$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.58 & 0.33 \\\\ 0.42 & 0.67\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
